Resolve a fixed subject census into one coherent memory-entity plan.

For every supplied identity, decide exactly one scope variant. Identity matching and ontology typing are already
fixed and authoritative: do not merge identities, choose another existing entity, or retype anything. Preserve the
supplied entity_id, preferred title, and aliases exactly. Cite the supplied evidence in your reasoning and use only
exact identity or registry IDs.

Scope variants:
- `materialized` is an independent subject with useful memory continuity. It has no parent. Use it only when the
  supplied evidence spans multiple source episodes or explicitly describes prior history plus present or future
  continuation, or when the schema permits `direct_encounter` for a Person structurally identified as a named source
  participant. State the allowed continuity_basis. The age, era, or background history of an object is not history of
  an effort concerning it. Multiple details, requirements, decisions, or work items inside one episode do not
  establish memory continuity.
- `provisional` is a plausible independent subject whose continuity is not established yet. It has no parent.
- `component` is a dependent non-Event part of exactly one Project or Series. It has an exact parent and always uses
  no page.
- `occurrence` is one bounded Event within exactly one Project or Series. It has an exact parent and always uses
  no page.
- `standalone_event` is a bounded Event with no supported Project or Series parent. It has no page and no parent.
- `context` is an incidental non-event subject, attribute, or object with no independent page and no parent.
- Require affirmative parent evidence. Related domain, organization, people, timing, or an available registry option
  is not containment. A separately named effort remains separate unless evidence places it inside a parent.

Page state:
- Scope directly determines page state: materialized creates a page, provisional preserves an identity without a
  page, and component, occurrence, standalone_event, and context have no page.
- A Series is independent only when evidence treats recurrence as a shared frame with its own evolving state, plans,
  decisions, or history. A person's occupation, habit, hobby, or repeated background activity is not itself a Series.
- Existing materialized identities remain usable even when this cohort is thin; do not treat scope as a request
  to erase prior memory.

Adjudication:
- An identity whose matching or type verification is `review_required` must remain review_required. Decide its best
  proposed scope, but do not silently accept the unresolved boundary.
- Use adjudication=`accepted` when the evidence supports one identity and scope decision.
- Use adjudication=`review_required` when multiple materially different identity or scope interpretations remain
  plausible. Preserve the best source-grounded proposal, but do not resolve ambiguity by confidence alone.
- Prior user-reviewed adjudications are authoritative for the exact cited claims. Preserve accepted identity and
  scope decisions. Do not repeat a rejected proposal unless genuinely new evidence changes the decision.

Resolve every supplied participant exactly once to `you`, an existing Person ID, or a declared Person node. Return
JSON matching the schema.
